    "title": "[Downstream] frontend: new markup error wcag/h37",
    "description": "Downstream's frontend check on !5 found this on the head build (4c2b115d674d) and not on the base build (7f2473276ae8). Started by @AlphaTechini.\n\n**Where it shows up**\n\n- `home_page`: wcag/h37 at `html > body > header > img`: <img> is missing required \"alt\" attribute\n- `explore_page`: wcag/h37 at `html > body > header > img`: <img> is missing required \"alt\" attribute\n- `repo_page`: wcag/h37 at `html > body > header > img`: <img> is missing required \"alt\" attribute\n- `issues_page`: wcag/h37 at `html > body > header > img`: <img> is missing required \"alt\" attribute\n\nPages were rendered in happy-dom with the app's own JavaScript, three times: base twice, then head. A check that moved between the two base runs is withheld, not reported here.\n\nNot checked: color-contrast, visual layout, real paint/CPU timing.\n\nThe `fix it` reply works on backend issues only; this one needs a human change.",
